Cave paintings from [[Ajanta Caves|Ajanta]], [[Bagh Caves|Bagh]], [[Ellora Caves|Ellora]] and [[Sittanavasal]] and temple paintings testify to a love of naturalism. Most early and medieval art in India is Hindu, Buddhist or Jain. A freshly made coloured floor design ([[Rangoli]]) is still a common sight outside the doorstep of many (mostly South Indian) Indian homes. [[Raja Ravi Varma]] is one of the classical painters from medieval India.

[[Pattachitra]], [[Madhubani painting]], [[Mysore painting]], [[Rajput painting]], [[Tanjore painting]] and [[Mughal painting]] are some notable Genres of Indian Art; while [[Nandalal Bose]], [[M. F. Husain]], [[S. H. Raza]], [[Geeta Vadhera]], [[Jamini Roy]] and B. Venkatappa<ref name="venka">Kamath (2003), p. 283</ref> are some modern painters. Among the present-day artists, Atul Dodiya, Bose Krishnamacnahri, [[Devajyoti Ray]] and Shibu Natesan represent a new era of Indian art where global art shows direct amalgamation with Indian classical styles. These recent artists have acquired international recognition. [[Jehangir Art Gallery]] in [[Mumbai]], [[Mysore Palace]] has on display a few good Indian paintings.

